<title>UK: Xenova up on Bristol-Myers alliance.</title>
<headline>Xenova up on Bristol-Myers alliance.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Xenova Plc shot up on Monday on news that the company had entered into a research collaboration with Bristol-Myers Squibb Co of the United States.</p>
<p>Xenova shares were trading at 295p, up 25p or 9.26 percent by 0854 GMT.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, Xenova will receive royalty payments from Bristol-Myers in return for research into the discovery of new drugs.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8958</p>
